h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 1.0 (build 949)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>The notes column has one place to type.</b> A composer card at the foot of the sidebar: the field grows as you write (Return sends, &#8679;Return breaks a line), and the row under it carries the <b>anchor chip</b> &#8212; the timecode the note lands on, following the playhead. Click the chip for <b>Whole review</b> instead; it returns to the frame after you send. The session-note field at the top is gone; whole-review notes lead the list in their own group.</li>
<li><b>The mic sits with the composer</b>, not on the transport bar; while recording, the row becomes a red <i>Recording 0:04</i> bar. V still records from anywhere.</li>
<li><b>Playing a voice note no longer loops the clip's audio</b> under it or after it.</li>
<li>The web page has the same composer (a drag handle above it makes the field taller), and its transport bar follows the app's order; typing in the web note field no longer fires hotkeys; Safari shows video and stills at the same gamma; voice notes send from Safari.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
